# Trivy suppressions.
#
# Every entry must have: the CVE, why it is not exploitable here, and an expiry.
# An unexplained or undated suppression is indistinguishable from ignoring the
# scanner, which defeats the point of having a blocking gate.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Example of an acceptable suppression:
#   # CVE-2024-00000: parser DoS in a transitive dev dependency. Not shipped in
#   # the runtime image (--omit=dev) and unreachable from any request path.
#   # Upstream fix tracked in #42.
#   CVE-2024-00000 exp:2026-12-31

# (empty - the image gate is currently passing with no suppressions)
